CODE 

class Solution(object):
    def lengthOfLastWord(self, s):
        sp = s.strip().split()
        ln = len(sp[-1])
        return ln

EXPLANATION
The logic is to first remove any extra spaces from the beginning and end of the string using strip(), and then use split() to separate the string into individual words. 
sp[-1] gets the last word from the list, and len(sp[-1]) finds the number of characters in that word. Finally, this length is returned as the answer.
